  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"113\" data-end=\"260\">The <strong data-start=\"117\" data-end=\"136\">Fluid Uric Acid</strong> test measures the concentration of uric acid in body fluids (e.g., pleural, synovial, peritoneal). It is primarily used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"262\" data-end=\"574\">\n<li data-start=\"262\" data-end=\"341\">\n<p data-start=\"264\" data-end=\"341\">Assist in the <strong data-start=\"278\" data-end=\"323\">differential diagnosis of joint disorders</strong> (especially gout)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"342\" data-end=\"395\">\n<p data-start=\"344\" data-end=\"395\">Help identify <strong data-start=\"358\" data-end=\"377\">gouty arthritis</strong> in synovial fluid</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"396\" data-end=\"486\">\n<p data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"486\">Evaluate <strong data-start=\"407\" data-end=\"434\">cell breakdown or lysis</strong> in body cavities (as in malignancies or infections)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"487\" data-end=\"574\">\n<p data-start=\"489\" data-end=\"574\">Support diagnosis of <strong data-start=\"510\" data-end=\"527\">effusion type</strong> when considered with other biochemical markers</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Elevated Levels &ndash; Clinical Implications</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Insight</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gout</strong></td>\n<td>High uric acid in synovial fluid; supports diagnosis along with presence of urate crystals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Tumor lysis syndrome</strong></td>\n<td>Massive cell breakdown increases uric acid in fluids; often with elevated potassium and phosphate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Malignancy-related effusions</strong></td>\n<td>Rapid cell turnover or necrosis may elevate uric acid levels in the affected fluid</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sepsis or infection</strong></td>\n<td>In rare cases, intense inflammation or tissue breakdown may lead to elevated levels</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
